#34500
The Abandoned Temple~
This temple built to a long-forgotten diety, has been abandoned for over
seven thousand years. For the last twenty-two hundred years, this long buried ruin has been
home to the gakrag.  The gakrag are a humanoid race who appear to be half ape
and half oxen.  They are quite large, enormously strong and fairly agile for
their size but their mental facilities are horribly limited, in fact, they
are absolute morons.  The most notable feature about them, though, is their
eyes.  Their pupils are the colorless white in white that usually indicates
blindness.  The gakrag are not, however, blind.  In fact, they have very keen
sight including infravision. The layout of the temple is simple but huge.  It
is intended as an experience area for higher level characters of any
alignment.  Written by Joe Hunter (Kord of RavenMud).
~
345 0 0 0 0 1 255 0
S
#34501
The Entry Hall~
You are standing in what was once an entryway into a temple of some kind.
To the south you see large double doors of an unknown material that were
apparently the outside opening of this building.  The architecture of the
door predates any on record making you realize this place is six thousand
years old at the very least. However, despite their age they look as if they
might have been built yesterday.  As deeply as the temple is buried, these
doors no longer open to the outside.  Instead, they open to a roughly carved,
dirt tunnel. The walls and floor are still structurally sound and the ceiling
is supported by ceiling-to-floor arches made of the same material as the
doors.  The walls throughout the hallway are covered with faded paintings of
an imposing black clad figure leading an army into battle.  Looking down at
the floor, you see tracks in the thin layer of dust covering the floor.  The
barefooted tracks are clearly humaniod but they definitely are not human.
From here, the hallway continues north and the crudely cut tunnel is to the
south where you catch the faint smell of fresh air.
~
345 109 0 0 0 1 255 0
D0
The hallway continues north.
~
~
