#34503
At a Corner in the Corridor~
You are standing at a corner in the corridor.  The wall are painted in an
abstract multi-colored design.  There are many different colors on the walls,
many of which have no name, but the dominant color is red of various shades.
Because of this strange pattern painted on the wall, it was impossible to see
this junction until you were right upon it.  The most amazing fact about the
design is no matter where you stand and look toward the corner, the pattern
on the near wall matches that of the far one, giving the illusion it is a
dead end.  Now that you know what you are looking at, you see this is, in
fact, a corner and the corridor extends to the north and east.
~
345 105 0 0 0 1 255 0
D0
The corridor extends to the north.
~
~
0 -1 34528
D1
The corridor extends to the east.
~
~
0 -1 34504
S
#34504
A Strange Corridor~
You are standing in a strange, multi-colored corridor.  Although many colors
are included in the pattern on the wall, red , and variations of red, is the
dominant color.  Because of the unique markings on the walls, you find it is
impossible to determine exactly how far the corridor extends.  It appears to
extend into infinity, but surely that must be an optical illusion.  Or is it?
The corridor extends to the east and west.
~
