#34587
The Center of the Temple~
Unlike the outer corridors of the temple, this room has no colorful patterns
turning the walls into optical illusions.  Instead, the inky blackness on the
the walls of this room appear to be eating the light.  The black paint used
in this room is not so much a color, as an absence of color.  At the northern
end of the room is a huge altar, and the room is filled with rows of benches.
It is obvious this was the worship chamber for the builders of this mammoth
structure. As you look around the room, the light-eating color of the walls,
floor and ceiling make it appear the benches, the altar and everything else
in the room is floating in a dark, gloomy void.  Considering the bright and
cheery color display throughout the rest of this building, you wonder why the
builders made this room so oppressive, if it was, in fact, they who did it.
The only way out is through the door you came in.
~
345 109 0 0 0 1 255 0
D2
There is a large opening to the south.
~
~
0 -1 34574
D5
The doorway leads down below.
~
door~
1 -1 34672
