#34599
At a Corner in the Corridor~
You are standing at a corner in the corridor.  The wall are painted in an
abstract multi-colored design.  There are many different colors on the walls,
many of which have no name, but the dominant color is purple of various
shades.  Because of this strange pattern painted on the wall, it was
impossible to see this junction until you were right upon it.  The most
amazing fact about the design is no matter where you stand and look toward
the corner, the pattern on the near wall matches that of the far one, giving
the illusion it is a dead end.  Now that you know what you are looking at,
you see this is, in fact, a corner and the corridor extends to the south and
west.
~
345 105 0 0 0 0 255 0
D2
The corridor extends to the south.
~
~
