The Sarcophagus Room~
You are standing in a simple, brown room.  The moment you walked in, you noticed
an overwhelming sense of pain and grief so deep you find it hard to function.
Compared to the rest of the temple, this room does not come close to being
worthy of this grand structure.  In the center of the room sits an undecorated 
sarcophagus on a granite slab roughly three feet tall.  Next to this is a 
granite pedastal holding a small, thin book.  There is nothing else in this
room.  The only apparent exit is back to the north.
